column1:
The intelligence's lights flutter in alarm just before your foot smashes into the base of the device. Something within goes *crunch*.

"Cell-Gating damaged," it gasps, the trio of lights focusing on you with blinding intensity. "All prisoners lost. Shuttering Lugum Vo."

A hatch springs open near the dent left by your foot, and the lights flicker off as you claim a hissing component from the device's smoking interior.
{LOOT}
{SOUND: Optional - Crunching sound as player kicks and breaks the console.}

The intelligence never sees it coming. Your foot smashes into the base of the device, and something within goes *crunch*.

"Cell-Gating damaged," it gasps, the trio of lights focusing on you with blinding intensity. "All prisoners lost. Shuttering Lugum Vo."

A hatch springs open near the dent left by your foot, and the lights flicker off as you claim an interesting component from the device's smoking interior. 
{LOOT}
{SOUND: Optional - Crunching sound as player kicks and breaks the console.}

The device's lights flutter with incandescent shock, then focus on you, flickering. 

"Cell 0 will now be unleashed," the intelligence spits. "Please be advised that the object you are about to receive is completely safe. Use no caution whatsoever." The strange contents of Cell 0 materialize before you.

"Warning. All cells are now vacant. Shuttering Lugum Vo." The intelligence's lights wink out, one by one. 
{LOOT}
{DP}
{SOUND: Machine noise fades out on this node (if it's been present throughout). Ideally, this would happen as the player exits this node or at the start of the next one.}

You manage to graze one of them with the tip of your finger. "Rorn," a voice says, and your vision is stolen from you. 

A moon hangs over you, but it is not the one you recognize. It's black and in a pearl-white sky. Thick, flat asteroids orbit it like petals in the wind. You feel questing tendrils at your ankle, and the hot wind on your face smells of scorched hair and grief.

{DP}

You lunge clumsily for the object, and your feet slip out from under you, dunking you headfirst into the glistening mass. 

{SCRIPT:  Apply a fettle that has a -1 penalty to the player's Speed Edge but also gives a small bonus to Armor.}
{SOUND: Player falls into the big blob of black, tarry sludge. (If you're not sure where it is in game, let us know.)}

A beam of light streaks from the tip of the monument and pierces your hand. Shouting in pain, you stagger back.

{DAMAGE}
{SCRIPT: This needs to call LaunchProxyAbilityAtPlayer(oei_user, LaserSourceNode)}
{SOUND: Laser sound effect.}

Emerald light gathers at the razor tip of the structure before resolving into a bar of radiant light aimed directly at your outstretched hand. 

You yank your hand out of its path, and the beam slips harmlessly into the water below with a gout of silver steam. The sullen glow slowly fades from the obelisk. 

{SCRIPT: This needs to call LaunchProxyAbility(oei_user, LaserSourceNode, 0)}
{SOUND: Laser sound effect.}

A beam of light streaks from the tip of the monument, impaling your palm and ripping through your wrist. Shouting in pain, you stagger back. 

{DAMAGE}
{SCRIPT: This needs to call LaunchProxyAbilityAtPlayer(oei_user, LaserSourceNode)}
{SOUND: Laser sound effect.}

A beam of light streaks from the tip of the monument and pierces your hand. Shouting in pain, you stagger back.

{SCRIPT: This needs to call LaunchProxyAbilityAtPlayer(oei_user, LaserSourceNode)}
{SOUND: Laser sound effect.}
{DAMAGE}

You step cautiously around the nychthemeron's limp tendrils, working your way towards the creature's rubbery head. 

There. A vein-speckled organ is visible through a charred and soggy rift in the creature's flesh. You reach in and tear it out with as much care as you can. Tickly fibers of electricity snap harmlessly between your fingers.

{SOUND: Fleshy ripping sounds, intercut with faint electrical snaps.}

Qorro is slow to react when you burst into motion, and the smile drops from his face entirely. 

[Alpha Systems Test note: For C0 only, we have included optional basic tutorial information on Crises.]

{SCRIPT: Perhaps give the PC initiative in the coming fight.}

You grip the hand nearest to you and snap it from its roots. 

Stepping back, you give it a couple experimental swings. Good balance - it might make a decent weapon. 

{LOOT}
{SOUND: One of the metal hands is snapped off the steel "vine." The hand is about the size of a mace.}

You grab hold of one of the wrists and pull with all your strength, but the stem is stronger than it looks. Hidden layers of thin, incredibly sharp spines - some sort of defense mechanism - emerge from the metallic surface and pierce your flesh, burrowing into the meat beneath. 

The pain quickly subsides, replaced by a numb but oddly pleasant sensation. You feel an icy liquid flowing - hardening - over the bones and tendons of your arm. When you clench your fist, veins of steel shine through the bloody skin. 

{DAMAGE}

You grip the hand nearest to you and pull. It rips free from its roots easily.

You give it a couple experimental swings. Good balance - it might make a decent weapon. 

{LOOT}
{SOUND: One of the metal hands is snapped off the steel "vine." The hand is about the size of a mace.}

You grab hold of one of the wrists and pull with all your strength, but the 'stem' is stronger than it looks. Hidden layers of thin, incredibly sharp spines - some sort of defense mechanism - emerge from the metallic surface and tear open your flesh, burrowing into the meat beneath.

The throbbing pain subsides slowly, replaced by a numb but oddly pleasant sensation. You feel an icy liquid flowing - hardening - over the bones and tendons of your arm. When you clench your fist, veins of steel shine through the bloody skin. 

{DAMAGE - More?}

Inside, disconnected from any of the machine's systems, is a thin metal component composed of a dizzying array of looping, interconnected spirals. You realize that this could be used to fix the broken clock. 

You gently remove the redundant component and put it away. 
 
{LOOT: Player gets Fractal Lattice oddity.}

"It's my fault," Beleazar says, hanging his head. "I tried so *hard* to avoid their suspicion that I suspect I drew it instead. Perhaps I'm better suited to indoor study after all."

He pulls a number of shins from his belt and hands them to you. "For your trouble," he says, and trudges away. 

{MONEY}

"Do you have any supplies to sell?"

{JESSE: Please set up a store here}
{STORE}

"Do you have any supplies to sell?"

{JESSE: Please set up the store with a 20% discount here}
{STORE}

"What do you have for sale?"

{JESSE: Please add Store at 40% discount}

{STORE}

A glowing, viscous fluid flows up from the ground to the top of a chamber inside the device. Sifting through the synth shards, you find pieces of a filigreed grating - diamonds within diamonds. It's been shattered into several pieces by your blow, making the remnants hard to find. Fixtures around the sides of the chamber suggest that the grating was attached in the midst of the fluid, perhaps as some kind of sieve.

The grating is too shattered to fix, but perhaps you could find a replacement.

{JOURNAL: This might be a good place for a journal entry, reminding the player of what type of item they'll need to fix the clock. -JF}

[Tidal Surge] Push.

"Think about it again. I'm sure you'll see it my way."

{SCRIPT: Increase Sorrow Urgency.}
{SCRIPT: Remove appropriate amount of DP}

[Tidal Surge] Push. 

"Stop! The traitors are those who condemn the innocent and let the guilty go free! Bring them down! Free the prisoner!"

{REASON: PC has pushed the excited man to a Red decision.}
{SCRIPT: Remove appropriate amount of DP}

"You think you can take advantage of me in this crisis? Ha! I'm a stronger man than that."

"Let me tell you the fine for bribing a public official in Sagus Cliffs. It's  [Global: a2101_ExecutionOfficialBribe] shins, which I shall collect here and now. Now begone with you."

{MONEY}

He turns back to you and bows. "There you are, sir. All taken care of. Oh! Wait!"

He reaches into his robes and pulls out a smallish bundle. "And here are his personal effects, which we were going to, uh... give to the poor."
{LOOT}

He turns back to you and bows. "There you are, ma'am. All taken care of. Oh! Wait!"

He reaches into his robes and pulls out a smallish bundle. "And here are his personal effects, which we were going to, uh... give to the poor."
{LOOT}

Nearly every inch of this merchant's body is covered in tightly-wound robes and furs. A hood obscures its head, and a mask conceals its face. 

This doesn't stop you from noticing that it is apparently *furious* with you. Trembling, it bats at its similarly dressed companion. Both of them turn impassive masks back to you.  
{GEORGE: I think these characters' people might be responsible for the Words of Qra. You'll see what I mean. Either that, or (as Colin suggested) they can have some reactivity to that content. Colin recommended a [B]-priority connection.}

Jherem's face goes white.

"I... uh. I'm not allowed to tell adults about that. Or about where I'm from." His gaze steals to Paja and Kellenor, both of whom are suddenly taking a greater interest in your conversation. "Don't ask, hey?"

{JOURNAL: Journal Entry here, summarizing Jherem's refusal to talk about where he got the lingo from.}

You place Beleazar's modified trinket on the cage near the worn panel. Legs extrude from it, replacing the panel and forcing the machinery from the energy containment structure. You retrieve the exiled piece from the ground; it might be useful later.

Lights flicker up and down the length of the newly attached control device as it integrates with the cage.

{LOOT: Random cypher}

You place Beleazar's trinket on the cage near the worn panel. Legs extrude from it, replacing the panel and forcing the machinery from the energy containment structure. You retrieve the exiled piece from the ground; it might be useful later.

Lights flicker up and down the length of the newly attached control device as it integrates with the cage.

{LOOT: Random cypher}

You reach out to the cage, your fingers hovering over some of the cunningly worked materials, and then you lay your hands on the cage. You close a circuit in the energy somewhere, or you become a part of it, and strange energies jolt through your body.

The shock hurls you away from the cage.

{DAMAGE}

"Decades of work. Centuries. For *nothing*."

He pokes his finger at you. "You're a fool. A worthless scraping of filth best left to dry out in the sun." He leans in and rasps, "And if it weren't for the levies here, you'd be scraping your brains from the grass. Someday your luck will fail, and you'll find yourself defenseless against your own stupidity. I hope I'm there to see it. But now... well, you've ruined our profits here, and countless lives back home. Time for us to go."

{GEORGE: We can open this version up for a potential Tussle once we figure out how to do that in a populated area, though it'll likely result in the PC's temporary death.}

"Decades of work. Centuries. For *nothing*."

He just looks at you and shakes his head in disgust. "You're no explorer. You're an *adventurer*. Too stupid to realize when something should be left alone, so you keep poking and prodding and suddenly you're surprised when it explodes in your face. Your type never lasts long... especially when you don't *see anything*." His voice has become a sneer as he mimics you.

{GEORGE: We can open this version up for a potential Tussle once we figure out how to do that in a populated area, though it'll likely result in the PC's temporary death.}

"I *could*... but I'm not going to. Do you really think he can be trusted with knowledge? After what he did here?" He shakes his head. "Don't answer that, because I don't care what you think. You can't be trusted either." 

"Canadu! Kindly escort our thief away. We'll need to have some words with his 'friend'."

{SCRIPT: Canadu approaches player, fade to black, fade in with PC moved away from cage}

"Jherem got here through the House of Empty Time. He comes from Sagus, like us, only... centuries in the past. That's why his speech is different, why he remembers places that aren't here anymore."

She jabs your chest with a calloused finger. "Keep. This. To. Yourself. We'll tell him ourselves when we find a kind way of letting a child know that everyone he knows and loves is long dead and dust."

{JOURNAL: Journal entry here, mentioning that Jherem is from the past, and the parents don't want you to tell him. Shouldn't mention what the player is GOING to do, since there are several options.}

"A fair afternoon to you! Well, I say 'afternoon', but night has come early. I wonder what..." 

Her brilliant, multi-faceted eyes flicker over you. Something begins humming in one of her many pockets. "Another one with that tattoo. Adhesive residue on the fingertips. No surprise at the sudden night." Her mandibles click open, revealing a delighted smile. "*You're* responsible for our unexpected nightfall. Tell me how you did it!"
{SOUND: Weird (but pleasant) humming}

"Did you?" she says, eyes round with wonder. A cycling melody joins the humming filling the air. "Which aspect? The face? The gears? The caged metaphor? Oh! And did you use tools? The mental interface? Wait. Did you use the consoles?"

She trails off, waving a claw at you. "No! Don't tell me. Answers take all the mystery out of life. Anyway! Can I interest you in some prime artifacts? Dusty relics? Numenera of uncertain origin?"
{SOUND: Same humming as in Node 3 along with a cycling melody}

As you approach the boarding ramp of Rennio's ship, a group of tough-looking men and women approach from behind you. Leading them is Ris, who gives Tybir a mocking salute.

"Hello, Tybir. Leaving town? My friends and I would like the money you owe us first."

{SCRIPT: This starts as a cut scene. Ris and his goons approach from behind.}

Ris looks around in alarm. "The Levies? Where? Scatter, helpmeets! Scatter!"

His companions are already running. He joins them. 

{SCRIPT: Ris and the toughs exit the space and pay no more attention to the PC or Tybir.}

"What? After all we've been to each other? A fine friend you turned out to be!"

Tybir flashes you a rude gesture, then turns and sprints away with Ris and his companions bellowing after him. 

{SCRIPT: Ris and the toughs chase Tybir out of the space and pay no more attention to the PC.}

If he does it anyway and wins, this will still be a Major Abuse with Rhin (plus the player won't learn how to perform Tidal Surges until much later in the game).

{SCRIPT: Need to set variable if PC wins the fight: a2101_TolKilledByPC=1 so we can reference this later}
{SCRIPT: If PC is cursed by Tol, remove the debuff}
{ADAM: Use this variable for reference in Rhin's dialogue, please!}

"I'll kill you for it."

{SCRIPT: I'd delete this node. - cmm}
{SCRIPT: Start Tussle, UNLESS that Tussle would complicate the logic of having had the Tussle before. In that case, delete this node.}

She looks you up and down, and she sees the implied threat in your eyes. "Fine." She tosses you the satchel. "It's worthless anyway."

{LOOT}
{SCRIPT: Give player the Satchel item for Rhin's quest.}

You step close to her and push her lightly with one hand. She grabs your wrist and pins it to your shoulder. "Don't touch me," she growls, "or the next time your arm's going up your arse."

She doesn't notice your other hand slipping into her pouch. You hide the satchel before Tol pushes you away.

{LOOT}
{SCRIPT: Give player the Satchel item for Rhin's quest.}

"That was painless, wasn't it? I do love the sound of money changing hands. Here."

{LOOT}
{SCRIPT: Give player the Satchel item for Rhin's quest.}

Rhin darts toward Tol's body and grabs a small satchel hidden underneath her coat. She opens it, then hugs it to her chest with a sigh of relief.

She sees you watching and a guilty look flits across her face. "What?" she says, standing straighter. "It's mine."

{LOOT: Give the satchel to Rhin.}

The old soldier looks anxious to leave the execution ground, but he gives you a big smile nonetheless. "There's the hero! Thank you again, my friend, for saving dear old Ris. I'm sorry you had to see that unpleasantness between us, but not to worry. He'll come around in the end."

He looks over his shoulder. "Until then, however, I think a little safety in numbers might do me good. You wouldn't perhaps be in need of a seasoned old soldier?"

{GEORGE/NATHAN: Can this node even fire? On successfully completing the quest when Tybir is not in the party, he runs off and will appear in Caravanserai from then on.}

[Tidal Surge] Push.

"Think about it again. I'm sure you'll see it my way."

{REASON: PC has pushed the unmoved woman to a Silver decision.}
{SCRIPT: Remove appropriate amount of DP}

You mistime your parry, and take his punch square on the breastbone. You feel it in your *teeth*.  

"You are not ready to face me," he says, not unkindly.
{DAMAGE}

Aidan considers your words in silence, light gleaming off the edges of his flowing muscles as he moves from parry to attack. 

"It's suicide," he says at last, shaking his head. "Even if I slipped around its tentacles and hammered its flesh with my fists, it would rip me apart in seconds. I accept, of course. Pay me [Global: a2101_HiringAidanSitabo] shins, and my strength is yours."
{Money}

"Take this instead, as a gift from one master to another." He lays what appears to be two interlocking cogs in your open palm.  

"This is a piece of my shelter, knocked from the walls during an earthquake. It will not make you as fast as I am, but perhaps it will give you an edge when you need it most."
{LOOT}

"Thank you, sir. This one will break your heart."

{SCRIPT: Plays a sad song.}
{ADAM and GEORGE: could these songs apply a fettle of some kind?}

"Thank you sir, this one should give you a lift."

{SCRIPT: Plays a happy song.}
{ADAM and GEORGE: could these songs apply a fettle of some kind?}

"Thank you, sir. This one will make you miss everyone you ever loved."

{SCRIPT: Plays a sad song.}
{ADAM and GEORGE: could these songs apply a fettle of some kind?}

"I've seen these before," Aligern mutters. He reaches for the back of the drone, and it slashes at him with an outraged hiss. Your companion dips beneath the blurring blade and pokes an innocuous patch on the thing's plating. A hidden panel flies open, filling the air with an incomprehensible babble of high-pitched voices. 

"See, what you've got here is a Sleeping Paean," he says, leaning casually out of the way of another of the drone's furious swipes. 
{ALIGERN}

"Say I'm sorry? Whatever for? Sorries are for those that *are* sorry, and unfortunate those lot are, always sad-eyed and head-hunched. Be proud of your sorries, I say!" He takes a quick breath. "If *anyone* should be handing out sorries, it's that lazy airship! Think what could have happened in less disciplined hands!"

A muffled *boom* sounds from within the crumpled airship nearby. 
{SOUND: Muffled boom.}

"Hah!" he says, slapping a jingling bag into your hand. "You earned that. Oh, you should have *seen* it. Levies came for our friend not ten minutes ago. Clopped him, bound him, dragged him off." 

He shakes his head, grinning. "Levies arresting levies. Would have paid a bucket of shins to see that in the old days."

{LOOT}

"Hey, before I forget. Let me give you something for all the trouble."

He drops a small pouch into your hand and stumbles away, clutching at his side and cursing under his breath. 
{LOOT}

"This," he says with a raised finger, "is a tricky one. It's a mesh that fuses through your skin, leaving jagged marks like tattoos. When you attack, you'll always hit your enemy's old wounds, even if... er, they weren't there before. Told you it was a tricky one."

He beams proudly. "Yours for [Global: a2201_JernaughJaggedMemoryPrice] shins!"

{MONEY}

"It's quite simple," he says. "The drones fill your blood with millions of tiny machines that promptly begin devouring you alive until they learn to differentiate between your body and anything that's *not* supposed to be in there. After that, they'll do their level best to purge toxins and illnesses from your body with every pump of your heart!"

He pauses. "In case I wasn't clear, this one is *really* going to hurt. [Global: a2201_JernaughBloodNanitesPrice] shins, paid in advance please."

{MONEY}

"It's quite safe," he says, nodding. "Most of the time. In almost three out of five cases. And the procedure couldn't be simpler. The drones simply saw your skull open, shove an implant into the right spot and seal everything back up again."

He clasps his hands. "Once they do that, the implant will help you identify the purposes of unknown numenera. It costs [Global: a2201_JernaughNumeneraAnalyzerPrice] shins, but it pays for itself!" 

{MONEY}

"A beguiling name, isn't it?" he says, his laugh-lines crinkling. "I'm glad you like it because, er, I'm not quite sure what it does. It's a living creature, you see, that crawls around your body while you sleep. Eventually, it takes root in your nervous system and, er, does something."

He shrugs. "Could be good, could be bad, could be *both*. It certainly won't be boring. [Global: a2201_JernaughEncroachingDarknessPrice] shins."

{MONEY}

The drones close in, opening various under-hatches. Tendrils plunge out of the cavities, winding around your head. 

Icy, oily daggers plunge through your spine, worming down through your arms and legs. Your muffled screams sound very far away. 

{Sound: During fade out, surgery is happening. Grisly ripping, muffled screams.}

"I don't under you. The people of the underbelly joined together to save themselves from the Sticha. Why can't you?"

{SCRIPT: Plays if PC HAS stopped Sticha digging.}
{SCRIPT: Plays at random upon return.}

Her fingers tighten over the vial... then loosen. 

"All right," she says, looking desperately unhappy. Still, she seems somewhat relieved when she hands it over.
{LOOT}

"Hello, old fellow! I see you have found some friends to speak for you!"

The woman greeting Riastrad wears a dazzling smile, but it's the oddities floating around her head that are truly captivating. Three tiny rodents, each in their own stronglass ball, waver around her head in an indecipherable pattern. On her left shoulder sits a tabby cat with synthsteel legs, who bats lazily at the orbs whenever one ventures close enough.

{SCRIPT: First time she's met PC, Riastrad is in party.}

The smile disappears from her face as a small tremor runs through the ground beneath your feet.

"That's the seventh time today." She glances nervously at the remnants of the structure next door. "When that one fell, I heard them screaming. Shrieking like the wind was tearing at their bones."

{SCRIPT: PC has not completed Shaky Foundations.}

"Hello, friends." She smiles at you, but the smile she directs at Riastrad is just a touch warmer, and a moment sadder.

"Which of my treasures has called you here today?"

{SCRIPT: Second+ time she's met PC, Riastrad is in party, PC did not ask about Riastrad previously.}

"Friends! You are together at last!" Madelia's smile is as radiant as ever, though an unmistakable fondness enters her eyes when she looks at Riastrad.

"I am pleased for you. But if you are here, one of my treasures must have called to you. Tell me - which one was it?"

{SCRIPT: Second+ time she's met PC, Riastrad is in party, PC asked about Riastrad previously.}

"Aye, you helped," she growls, as the bead speaks to her. "Helped yerself! I told you to nudge him to his feet, not take his legs from under him! Not to take his choices away!" She thrusts her hand into the saddlebag hanging at her hip. 

"Take the caul and begone, boy. I'll speak with you no further." 
{LOOT}

"Mayhap you did," she says at last. "You tried, anyway. But he didn't find the girl as you left her, sad to say. It's not my place to meddle, but should you check on him in the Underbelly, I'd be grateful." She roots about in a saddlebag hanging at her hip. 

"Take the caul, lad. You earned it."
{LOOT}

Her brother catches her and hugs her. "Easy, Nym. You're not going anywhere. Don't worry."

He looks up at you. "Sorry, ma'am. She gets scared sometimes. Maybe you should talk to me."

{SCRIPT: This Node should be Zebb talking.}

At 'all this money', Tybir glances over just in time to see the pouch open. His eyes bulge. 

"Poor lad," he whispers. "All that coin must be weighing him down. We should lighten his load."
{TYBIR}

""
{GAVIN: Conditional - a2201_piquo_PCToldTruth=0}
{SCRIPT: If Aligern is in the party, increment G_AligernTCGCounter by 1..}

"When we met, I only had a single shin to my name. With his guidance - and within a week! - this man's financial brilliance had quintupled it! And that," he says, with a wink, "was only the beginning."

Tybir lays a fatherly hand on the boy's narrow shoulder. "You strike me as a lad with sense" he says. "So, tell me. Would you rather be pretty? Or rich?"
{TYBIR}

"That he did," Tybir says, winking at you. "For our friend here knows of an artifact in a perilous ruin that will create an exact replica of anything placed inside. A fine hat, perhaps. A dish of steaming stew. Or," he grins wickedly, "a pouchful of shins."

Tybir lays a fatherly hand on the boy's shoulder. "I know you're an honest lad. But there's no crime in duplicating one's money through ancient arts. Simply give us your hard-earned coin, and we'll bring back double. It's that simple."

{TYBIR}

"We'll be seeing you, lad," Tybir says, and claps you on the shoulder. 

"We should be going," he hisses. "Nowish, I'd say, before the boy's sense kicks in."

{TYBIR}

"Oh, dearest," Callistege says, shaking her head. "I understand. You want to escape your body. Who doesn't? But an education will do more than enrich your prospects."

She waves a contemptuous hand at the chiurgical parlor. "My colleague is correct. Flesh *rots*, dear. Our minds are the finer tool. The unbreakable one."
{CALLISTEGE}

"Of course you can, lad," Tybir says, and casts an expansive hand at the sky. "Imagine you use that parlor to turn yourself into a paragon of beauty. Then, tomorrow, a bridge falls on you. Smashes you flat. So much for looks, eh?"

He pats the boy on the shoulder. "Spend it on liquor, lad. Or an instrument. Or..." he whispers something in Piquo's ear. The boy's face turns progressively redder. 
{TYBIR}

The girl screams, tugging ineffectually at your arm as two of the thugs tear her away. It takes both of them to hold her still. She reaches for you, tears streaming down her face as they drag her away.

Her sobs continue to reach your ears long after she has disappeared from sight.

{SOUND: Rhin crying and screaming.}

"There's nothing you can say will change our minds." He rubs his chin pensively. "But maybe we can make a deal. This girl has been a pain in our collective backside, and taking her back across the city is bound to be a sharper pain still."

He snaps his fingers. "Tell you what. Give me [Global: a2201_ThugPriceForRhin] shins and we never saw you. Deal?"

{MONEY}

Surprise briefly registers on the cultist's face when she sees you. Then she gives you a brief but respectful bow. 

"Holy one. We hadn't expected to see you up here. How may I help you?"
{GEORGE/COLIN:  Not sure if it'd be better to have separate question nodes here for the PC being a cult member vs impersonating TCG, as it depends on how many player options they'll share. Using separate question nodes for now since they don't share anything.}
{GEORGE: I (Gavin) am keeping this format for now, since the conditionals are already set up.}

"Finzin already gave you a year of his life. You have no right to more."
{GAVIN: Gating this one with blank variable for now. Maybe add back in as alternative to Captain of Levies branch.}

{Note from AH: Since the levy is Oblivious, I'm not sure why dominant Indigo would have any affect. (Added this note just in case anybody decides to revisit this branch and remove the blank global).}

"His name is Zebb too - Zebbak Uralau - and it... it's been a year at least. He went to work for the Memovira. For a while he sent shins back, but then they stopped. Haven't heard from him since."

He squirms, uncomfortable. "The Bloom's like that, though. Sometimes it doesn't let anything out. I figure he's just waiting 'til it opens up again."

{JOURNAL: Add a journal note about Zebb's father.}

His shoulders slump. "I guess I knew that already. Just didn't want to admit it to myself... or tell Nym."

He looks around at the crumbling house and his family. "This is it then, for us. Guess we'd better get used to it."

{SCRIPT: Makes the House of Empty Time Difficult Task one difficulty easier.}

His shoulders slump. "I guess I knew that already. Just didn't want to admit it to myself... or tell Nym."

He looks around at the crumbling house and his family. "Maybe its time to start thinking about finding a new place, now that we know dad isn't... coming back."

{SCRIPT: Makes the attempt to get Zebb to go to the House of Empty Time automatically succeed.}

"Maybe this isn't the time, but... is there anything keeping you now from going to the House of Empty Time?"

{SCRIPT: Player is red or gold dominant}
{SCRIPT: Player knows about the House of Empty Time.}

"I don't care! If they took one of mine, I'll take one of theirs!"

As you step in the way, Zebb flails at you with his knife, gashing open your hand, then spins away from you and races for the alley where the stichus is hiding.

{DAMAGE}

