{SOUND: A gasp, heavy, masculine, not a gasp of surprise but more of a choking gasp, a bit wet, if that makes sense - like someone coming out of a nightmare or even a coma.}

You try to will yourself awake, but Inifere clings to the darkness, its solace and solitude, and forces your flesh back into a slumber.

So this is how it will be: a test of wills. But you are no novice to such struggles, and Inifere is no Kalaghat Anvor. In the end, even the Tabaht general could not stand against you. Inifere whimpers in the shadows of your mind - he cannot defy you either.

