For a week you wear the Mindeye behind your ear, recording every moment of your life - the drudgery, the abuses, both minor and major, from your Sona masters and their Bayan enforcers. The slights, the insults, the shoves, the casual threats, the stories of the other Nil, the fear of losing your job, the fear of dying to keep it, your dreams of freedom, your rage, your sorrow, your infrequent joys, your courage, your cowardice, your pettiness, your simple humanity. 

Several times during the week, Aurigan accosts you, leering, joking, insulting you, making unwanted advances, threatening you with violence. You wonder how he will react to being abused by himself.

