The secret to peace is empathy. If we could all live for a time in our enemies' heads, and if they could live in ours, then conflict would be impossible, for they would understand our pain and we would understand theirs. Our life experiences would be shared. We would be family. Closer than family. We would be one. And who but a madman could make war upon himself?

{SCRIPT: Is it possible to set the text of the book in italic, or differentiate it from the normal discriptive text of the Mere?}
