Under heavy guard, and with force shields and temporal randomizers in place, Lovac escorts you to the edge of No Man's Land. It is scarred with trenches and thick with roiling smoke, but more unnerving are the drifting shards of time and reality that cross it like summer storms. In one, great armies move. In another, towering constructs with glowing eyes burn the homes of fleeing villagers. And on and on. 

Lovac points ahead. "There - somewhere - is your path. Use your instincts to hunt this villain down, but take care. Too many jumps and you will enter realities where the storm is fading, the shards closing. You could be trapped in a distant reality with no way back."

