You prime the cypher and overhand it toward the heater crew. A perfect throw. They stare in horror as the ovoid lands among them, then it implodes, sucking all air and matter within a ten meter radius into a single point. The heater and most of the crew vanish in a deafening thunderclap as the surrounding air rushes in to fill the space they no longer occupy. Unfortunately, one of the snipers was just out of the radius, and he starts shrieking and firing your way.

You duck into cover and pick him off as he pops up for a shot, but his warnings have been heard. Shouting is coming from both the skirmishers and the launcher crew. 

{SOUND: Sonic boom.}

As you try to decide which way to run, the launcher crew acts, and the bright arc of an incendiary cypher rises above you, then drops down right toward your position. 

You shout at your squad to scatter, but it's too late. The cypher explodes ten meters over your heads, showering liquid fire down on everything within a twenty meter radius of you. You are covered in stripes of it that burn you instantly to the bone. Beside you, Vostiel staggers around, his head a charred lump. You reach for him, but your hands are on fire. 

{SOUND: Fiery explosion.}

As you shoot the survivors, a roar distracts you. A pair of dark, loping shapes are bounding for you. Frilled bauls! The skirmishers' hidden weapon!

You and Vostiel cook one with your beamers, but the other downs one of your troopers and tears her throat out before your squad can kill it. Worse, fighting it gives the other squads time to find you. The beam of the heater sweeps your way. The bright arc of an incendiary cypher drops down toward your position. 

You shout at your crew to scatter, but it's too late. The round explodes over your heads, showering liquid fire upon you. Vostiel staggers past you, his head a charred lump. You reach for him, but your hands are on fire. 

{SOUND:Roaring lions.}
{ART: Illustration - Frilled bauls}

A moment later the gases clear, revealing a silent and lifeless scene. Not a single enemy survived. The battle, as the Aeon Priest had promised, is over before it could begin. 

Your men cheer and raise the Aeon Priest on their shoulders. He'll probably be the only one rewarded for this, but at least it's still a victory.

{SOUND: Rain and distant cheers.}
{ART: Illustration - Blowing up the Ambushers}

It's a long and grueling battle, with casualties on both sides, but finally, after your scouts eliminate the ambusher's launcher crew, and your snipers knock out their heater, the enemy captain calls a retreat and you win the day. A decisive victory, if not a glorious one, but more importantly, you kept the priest and his artifact safe and out of enemy hands. 

As your company marches once more into the endless silver rain, Landi salutes you and Vostiel gives you a nod of respect. Even the little priest thanks you, though he still insists he could have ended the battle quicker all by himself. Surely, Commander Rekken will have nothing to complain about this day.

{SOUND: Battle sounds.}
{ART: Illustration - Victorious Captain}

Your squad spreads out and takes cover in the rubble along the path of the enemy patrols, then takes them out as they pass with silent sliver spitters tipped with arcane chemicals that paralyze them before they can sound the alarm.

