{SOUND: Energy weapon fire.}

Vostiel salutes, then swallows. "Tell... tell Landi I'll miss her disapproving glare. Always made my little heart go pitter pat."

He turns and lays himself behind the ridge so his head is level with it, then pokes the barrel of his beamer through the weeds that cover it. You and your last squad member, Alvoosh, stay with him as he waits for the construct to turn its eye his way. Finally, he exhales and fires, and instantly his head explodes. It almost seems as if he shot himself.

You look up. The construct is flat on its face, smoke and sparks coming from its shattered head, while the troopers in the enclosure next to it are firing in all the wrong directions. {SOUND: Robot's powerful beam weapon}

As the silver rain washes Vostiel's boiling blood down the incline of the ridge, you pick up his long range beamer and then you and Alvoosh get down to the slow but certain work of picking off the last four defenders one by one. 

Glory will be yours for taking the monolith this day, and a promotion too, most likely. Only you will know if they were deserved or not. 

{SOUND: All sounds fade except the rain.}
